{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 61, :comments ["<b>And Rebekah arose, and her maidens</b> — Scripture relates that after they granted permission for Rebekah and her nurse and Abraham's servant and his men to go, Rebekah arose and called her maidens, and they mounted the camels and went after the man, for he guides the way before them." "And the sense of <b>And the servant took Rebekah, and went</b> is to tell of his zeal, for after he went out from the city and all the women went after him, the servant took Rebekah with him — he would not part from her, to guard her on the way from every stumbling block. And Rabbi Abraham said (Ibn Ezra on Genesis 24:61) that the meaning is that he was walking with Rebekah and did not perceive until Isaac came and encountered him."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:34:19.136526246Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}